    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The ukulele is a guitar-like musical "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "instrument",
            "zh": "乐器"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " from "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Hawaii",
            "zh": "夏威夷"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". People often call it by its nickname: the uke. How much do you know about this instrument?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "King David Kalakaua once "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "ruled",
            "ref": "v-rule"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the Kingdom of Hawaii. Back then, ukuleles were often seen at "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "royal",
            "zh": "皇家的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " events. The king also asked people to learn how to play the ukulele. And he learnt how to play it himself!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "You may have heard that “ukulele” means “jumping "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "flea",
            "ref": "v-flea"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "” in "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Hawaiian",
            "zh": "夏威夷语"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". But Hawaii’s last queen "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "translated",
            "ref": "v-translate"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the word as “gift from afar”."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Early ukulele "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "strings",
            "ref": "v-string"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " were made of "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "gut",
            "zh": "肠线,尤用羊肠制成"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Today, most ukulele strings are made of "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "nylon",
            "zh": "尼龙"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". But you can still find gut strings in some shops."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The ukulele comes in three main shapes: a "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "figure",
            "ref": "v-figure"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " 8, a pineapple and a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "paddle",
            "zh": "船桨"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "n1",
        "type": "note",
        "title": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Did you know?"
          }
        ],
        "content": [
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "尤克里里是美国夏威夷的一种传统弹拨乐器，形似一把小吉他，最常见的为四弦，亦可见五弦、六弦甚至八弦。19世纪70年代，一种形状相似的葡萄牙乐器传入夏威夷，后演变为尤克里里。"
            }
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
